Let me think about how averages work. The average of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by how many numbers there are. So, if I can find the sum of the remaining numbers and the number of remaining numbers, I can set up an equation to solve for the erased number.

Let me denote the original number of numbers as n. So, the original sum of numbers from 1 to n is given by the formula S = n(n + 1)/2. That's a standard formula for the sum of the first n natural numbers.

After erasing one number, say x, the new sum becomes S - x, and the number of numbers becomes n - 1. The average of the remaining numbers is (S - x)/(n - 1) = 35 7/17.

Hmm, 35 7/17 is a mixed number. Let me convert that to an improper fraction to make calculations easier. 35 is 35*17/17, which is 595/17. Adding 7 gives 602/17. So, the average is 602/17.

So, (S - x)/(n - 1) = 602/17.

