The sum of the reciprocal geometric progression is found by recognizing that the new progression has a common ratio of \( \frac{1}{r} \). Using the sum formula for a geometric series, we express the new sum in terms of the original sum \( s \) and simplify to find that the new sum is \( \frac{s}{r^{n-1}} \).

