To find the smallest positive number among the given options, we need to evaluate each expression numerically. The options are:

A) \(10 - 3\sqrt{11}\)  
B) \(3\sqrt{11} - 10\)  
C) \(18 - 5\sqrt{13}\)  
D) \(51 - 10\sqrt{26}\)  
E) \(10\sqrt{26} - 51\)

Using approximate values for the square roots:
- \(\sqrt{11} \approx 3.3166\)
- \(\sqrt{13} \approx 3.6055\)
- \(\sqrt{26} \approx 5.0990\)

Calculating each option:
- A) \(10 - 3\sqrt{11} \approx 10 - 9.9498 = 0.0502\)
- B) \(3\sqrt{11} - 10 \approx 9.9498 - 10 = -0.0502\) (negative)
- C) \(18 - 5\sqrt{13} \approx 18 - 18.0275 = -0.0275\) (negative)
- D) \(51 - 10\sqrt{26} \approx 51 - 50.990 = 0.010\)
- E) \(10\sqrt{26} - 51 \approx 50.990 - 51 = -0.010\) (negative)

The positive results are:
- A) \(\approx 0.0502\)
- D) \(\approx 0.010\)

Comparing these, the smallest positive number is option D.

