First, I set up the coordinate system with C at (0,0), A at (30,0), and B at (0,16). The hypotenuse AB has the equation y = (-8/15)x + 16.

For circle O₁, which is tangent to the x-axis (y=0) and hypotenuse AB, its center is at (h₁, r). The distance from (h₁, r) to AB must be r.

Similarly, for circle O₂, which is tangent to the y-axis (x=0) and hypotenuse AB, its center is at (r, k₂). The distance from (r, k₂) to AB must be r.

