Wait, that makes sense. So, the total time from setting the fuse to hearing the blast is T seconds. The blast occurs at 30 seconds, and the sound takes T - 30 seconds to reach him. During that T - 30 seconds, the powderman is still running away at 8 yards per second.

So, the distance the powderman has run by the time he hears the blast is 8 * T yards. But the sound has to cover the distance he ran in T seconds, but it's actually the distance he ran in T - 30 seconds because the sound starts at 30 seconds.

