I know that 1 yard is 3 feet, so 1080 feet per second is equal to 1080 / 3 = 360 yards per second. So, the sound travels at 360 yards per second.

Therefore, the distance the sound has traveled is 360 * (T - 30) yards. But this distance should be equal to the distance the powderman has run, which is 8T yards. So, I can set up the equation:

