Wait, no, actually, for three vertices, the number of transitive tournaments is 2. Because you can have either A->B, B->C, and A->C, or A->C, C->B, and A->B. Wait, no, that's the same as the first one. Maybe I'm overcomplicating. Let me look it up in my mind. I think for n=3, the number of strongly connected tournaments is 2. So, S(3)=2.

