Alicia earns $20 per hour, and 1.45% of this is deducted for local taxes. To find the tax in dollars:

\[
\text{Tax in dollars} = \left( \frac{1.45}{100} \right) \times 20 = 0.0145 \times 20 = 0.29 \text{ dollars}
\]

Converting this to cents:

\[
0.29 \text{ dollars} \times 100 = 29 \text{ cents}
\]

Thus, Alicia pays 29 cents per hour in local taxes.

