Carrie's garden measures 6 feet by 8 feet, giving an area of:
\[ 6 \times 8 = 48 \text{ square feet} \]

She plants 4 strawberry plants per square foot, resulting in:
\[ 48 \times 4 = 192 \text{ plants} \]

Each plant yields an average of 10 strawberries, so the total number of strawberries harvested is:
\[ 192 \times 10 = 1920 \]

Thus, the final answer is:
