Since \( x \) is less than 180 degrees, we have:
\[ 2017 < (n-2) \times 180 < 2197 \]

Dividing by 180:
\[ 11.205 < n - 2 < 12.205 \]

Thus, \( n - 2 = 12 \) (since \( n \) must be an integer), so \( n = 14 \). The actual sum is:
\[ (14 - 2) \times 180 = 12 \times 180 = 2160 \]

The forgotten angle is:
\[ 2160 - 2017 = 143 \]

Thus, the measure of the forgotten angle is \(\boxed{D}\).

